# Testing Rules

## Coverage requirements

- Every new API endpoint must have at least one integration test
- Every utility function must have unit tests covering:
  - Happy path
  - Edge cases (empty input, nulls, boundaries)
  - Error cases
- Business logic functions: 100% branch coverage

## Test structure

```
describe('[unit under test]', () => {
  describe('[scenario / method]', () => {
    it('should [expected behavior] when [condition]', () => {
      // Arrange
      // Act
      // Assert
    })
  })
})
```

## Test data

- Use factories/fixtures, never hardcoded magic IDs
- Tests must not depend on execution order
- Tests must not share mutable state

## What not to test

- Third-party library internals
- Framework behavior (e.g., Next.js routing)
- Implementation details — test behavior, not internals

